    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.motif_census - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.motif_census.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.motif_census()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Count occurrences of all non-isomorphic connected subgraphs of a given size.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.motif_census()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Count occurrences of all non-isomorphic connected subgraphs of a given size.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.motif_census()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Count occurrences of all non-isomorphic connected subgraphs of a given size.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCount occurrences of all non-isomorphic connected subgraphs of a given size.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L40499-L40657){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.motif_census(size=3)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Motif census](../assets/graphs/motif-census.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: the seven-node graph from the dominating set figures, a pendant 1, triangle 2, 3, 4, a bridge 4–5, and triangle 5, 6, 7. Right: the two connected three-node motifs with their counts: 2 triangles and 6 induced paths, where a path is a triangle with its third edge missing (dashed).\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nEnumerates every connected induced subgraph of `size=` nodes, classifies each by its\nisomorphism class, and returns the counts. This is the standard *motif census* used in\nnetwork biology to characterize local connectivity patterns.\n\n\"Induced\" means that a group of nodes is classified by *all* the edges among them, so\nthree mutually linked nodes count once as a `\"triangle\"` and are not also counted as\npaths. Only connected groups are counted (in directed graphs, weakly connected: edge\ndirection is ignored for the connectivity test but kept for the classification). The\ncounts are a fingerprint of a network's local wiring, useful for:\n\n- comparing the small-scale structure of different networks\n- spotting over-represented building blocks such as feed-forward loops in gene\n  regulation or closed triads in social networks\n- providing the observed counts for a significance test (see `motif_significance()`)\n\nMotif classes are named as follows. For undirected graphs with `size=3` the classes are\n`\"triangle\"` and `\"path\"`. For undirected graphs with `size=4` the fully connected and\none-edge-missing classes are `\"clique_4\"` and `\"near_clique_4\"`; other four-node shapes\nget names of the form `\"motif_4e<edges>_k<key>\"`, where `<edges>` is the number of edges\nand `<key>` is an internal canonical code that distinguishes shapes with the same edge\ncount (e.g., a star from a path). Directed motifs are always named `\"motif_<size>_<key>\"`.\nClasses that do not occur are omitted from the result.\n\nEvery combination of `size=` nodes is checked, so the cost grows roughly as `n^3` for\n`size=3` and `n^4` for `size=4`. This is fine for graphs with a few hundred nodes but\nbecomes slow on large graphs. Edge weights are ignored.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[size]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[3]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Number of nodes in each motif. Must be `3` (default) or `4`; any other value raises a\n    `ValueError`. Four-node motifs reveal richer patterns (squares, stars, near-cliques)\n    but are considerably more expensive to count.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[str, int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A `{motif_class: count}` dictionary, with the classes in sorted order of their names.\n    If the graph has fewer than `size=` nodes, the dictionary is empty.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `size=` is not `3` or `4`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~motif_significance`) \n\n:   Compare the counts with degree-preserving random graphs.\n\n[](`~triadic_census`) \n\n:   Count the 16 types of triad in a directed graph.\n\n[](`~count_triangles`) \n\n:   Count the triangles at each node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\n`A`, `B` and `C` form a triangle, and `D` hangs off `C`. The two groups that include `D`,\n`A`-`C`-`D` and `B`-`C`-`D`, are open paths, so the census finds one triangle and two\npaths:\n\n::: {#dad73d73 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"A\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")]\n)\ngraph.motif_census()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{'path': 2, 'triangle': 1}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The six shapes on four nodes\n\nFour nodes can be connected in six ways. Only the complete one and the one missing an\nedge get readable names; a graph made of one copy of each shape shows which code stands\nfor which of the others:\n\n::: {#80989a32 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nshapes = {\n    \"star\": [(1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4)],\n    \"path\": [(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4)],\n    \"square\": [(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4), (4, 1)],\n    \"paw\": [(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 1), (3, 4)],\n    \"near clique\": [(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4), (4, 1), (1, 3)],\n    \"clique\": [(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4), (4, 1), (1, 3), (2, 4)],\n}\ngallery = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(f\"{name} {u}\", f\"{name} {v}\")\n     for name, pairs in shapes.items() for u, v in pairs]\n)\ngallery.set_node_attrs(\n    \"shape\", {label: label.rsplit(\" \", 1)[0]\n              for label in gallery.get_node_df()[\"label\"]}\n)\ngallery.motif_census(size=4)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n{'clique_4': 1,\n 'motif_4e3_k591': 1,\n 'motif_4e3_k669': 1,\n 'motif_4e4_k1782': 1,\n 'motif_4e4_k735': 1,\n 'near_clique_4': 1}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#adc50a9b .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngallery.plot(color_by=\"shape\", height=300)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"300\" viewBox=\"69.7 16.0 672.1 288.1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"69.7\" y=\"16.0\" width=\"672.1\" height=\"288.1\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<line x1=\"219.3\" y1=\"140.7\" x2=\"176.8\" y2=\"142.3\" stroke=\"#59a14f\" stroke-width=\"1.56\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<line x1=\"219.3\" y1=\"140.7\" x2=\"176.8\" y2=\"142.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"8.0\" pointer-events=\"stroke\" data-edge=\"11-10-0\" data-attrs='{\"id\": 8, \"edge\": \"10 \\u2014 11\"}'/>\n<line x1=\"237.6\" y1=\"126.8\" x2=\"252.1\" y2=\"82.1\" stroke=\"#59a14f\" stroke-width=\"1.56\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<line x1=\"237.6\" y1=\"126.8\" x2=\"252.1\" y2=\"82.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"8.0\" pointer-events=\"stroke\" data-edge=\"11-12-1\" data-attrs='{\"id\": 9, \"edge\": \"11 \\u2014 12\"}'/>\n<line x1=\"314.8\" y1=\"89.2\" x2=\"385.2\" y2=\"137.8\" stroke=\"#4e79a7\" stroke-width=\"1.56\" st